381		The tuple $\mathsf{qldparams} = (q,m,d)$ is \emph{admissible} if $d \ge 1$, $q$ is an admissible field size (Definition~\ref{def:admissible-size}), and $m$ divides $q$. Since an admissible field size satisfies $q \ge 2$, the divisibility forces $m \ge 1$, so an admissible tuple has all entries positive.
